1479 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Living things are all around us. Plants, animals and human beings are examples of living things. Although they are different from one another, all living things need certain things to survive, grow and stay healthy.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1480 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Living things need food, water, air and shelter. These things help them grow, get energy, protect themselves and continue living.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1481 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (When we observe plants and animals around us, we can see that they depend on their surroundings for what they need. A plant in a garden needs water and sunlight to grow. A goat on a farm needs food, water and a safe place to rest. Human beings also need food, water, air and shelter to live.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Food)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Food is one of the important things that living things need. Food gives living things energy to grow, move and carry out their daily activities. Human beings eat different kinds of food such as rice, maize, fruits, vegetables, fish and meat. These foods help our bodies grow strong and healthy. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Animals also need food to survive. Goats eat grass and leaves. Chickens eat grains and seeds. Some animals eat other animals for food.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Plants also need food, but they make their own food using sunlight, water and air. The food made by plants helps them grow and stay healthy.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Without food, living things become weak and may not grow properly.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Water)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Water is another important need of living things. All plants and animals need water to survive. Human beings drink water to keep their bodies healthy. Animals also drink water to stay alive. Farmers provide water for animals on farms.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (Plants need water to grow. Water helps plants carry nutrients from the soil to different parts of the plant. When plants do not get enough water, their leaves may dry up and the plant may die. We should use water carefully and avoid wasting it because living things depend on it.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
