1834 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1109 0 R
/E (Everything around us is made of materials. Materials can be found in different forms. Some materials are hard and keep their own shape, some can flow and take the shape of their containers, while others spread out and cannot be easily seen.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
1835 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1109 0 R
/E (The different forms of materials are called states of materials. The three common states of materials are solids, liquids and gases. We can identify the state of a material by observing its shape, size and how it behaves.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
