2091 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (Weather describes the condition of the air and sky around us at a particular time. When we look outside, we may notice that the day can be bright and hot, cloudy, rainy or windy. These changes in the weather affect the activities we do every day.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
2092 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (Weather helps us decide what clothes to wear, what activities we can do and how we take care of our surroundings. Farmers also observe the weather because it helps them know when to plant crops and take care of their farms.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2093 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (We can observe the weather by looking at the sky, feeling the temperature, noticing rainfall and watching how the wind moves things around us. There are different types of weather that we experience in our environment. Some common types are sunny weather, rainy weather and windy weather.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
2094 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (Sunny Weather)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [9]
>>
