2095 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (Sunny weather happens when the Sun shines brightly in the sky. During sunny weather, the sky is usually clear, and there may be little or no clouds. On a sunny day, we may feel heat from the Sun. People often wear light clothes and use hats or umbrellas to protect themselves from too much sunlight.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
2096 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/E (The Sun is important because it gives us light and heat. Plants need sunlight to grow, and people use sunlight for activities such as drying clothes and drying some foods.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
2097 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
